    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d732">

                <pb facs="1000" n="986" sameAs="frus:frus1944v06/pg986"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.543/277: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-04-27T09:00:00+07:00">April 27, 1944—9
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 27—6:17 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>736. Reference my 640, April 12, 11 a.m., regarding reregistration of trademarks.
                    I mentioned this matter April 25 to Foreign Minister<anchor n="7"
                        xml:id="d732-f1"/> and Political Vice Minister<anchor n="8" xml:id="d732-f2"
                    /> who inquired what is being done in other countries where reregistration may
                    not be readily possible due to war time conditions. If information on this point
                    is forthcoming from Department, I believe we may be able to do something here to
                    alleviate the situation.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
